.page base64 1 encode or decode base64 data

# SYNOPSIS
*base64* [*-d*] [*-w* _COLS_] [_FILE_]

# DESCRIPTION
`base64` encodes _FILE_ (or standard input) as base64 text and writes it in lines of 76 characters. With `-d` it decodes: every character that is not part of the base64 alphabet is ignored, which also makes it forgiving about line breaks.

# OPTIONS
@ *-d*
    Decode.
@ *-w* _COLS_
    Wrap encoded lines after _COLS_ characters. 0 turns wrapping off. The default is 76.
@ *-i*
    Accepted and ignored.

# EXAMPLES
    echo -n hi | base64
    echo aGk= | base64 -d
    base64 -w 0 /Hakurei/etc/hostname

# SEE ALSO
xxd(1), md5sum(1)
